---
/**
 * /wallpapers/self-love — SEO landing page for the Self Love category.
 * Chrome page (ChromeLayout), fully indexable, links through to the real
 * photos at /gallery#soft-life (world key `soft`, slug `soft-life`).
 */
import ChromeLayout from '../../layouts/ChromeLayout.astro';
---

<ChromeLayout
  title="Self-Love & Affirmation Wallpapers | motivationalwallpaper.com"
  description="Gentle affirmation wallpapers to help you be kinder to yourself, one lock screen at a time"
>
  <h1>Self-Love & Affirmation Wallpapers</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    A gentler voice to greet you every time you check your phone.
  </p>

  <p>
    Most of us are harder on ourselves than we'd ever be on a friend, and
    that inner voice tends to get loudest exactly when we're already
    struggling. These self-love wallpapers are built to interrupt that
    pattern in a small, low-effort way — soft blush and cream tones paired
    with a gentle affirmation, sitting on the one screen you look at more
    than any other. You don't have to journal or meditate to benefit; you
    just have to unlock your phone the way you already do.
  </p>
  <p>
    The words lean toward permission rather than pressure — you're allowed
    to begin again, you're allowed to take up space, you're allowed to be a
    work in progress. It's a category for anyone rebuilding their
    relationship with themselves after a hard year, a breakup, a season of
    burnout, or just quietly deciding they're done speaking to themselves
    unkindly. Small, repeated moments of gentleness add up — this is one
    of the easiest ones to build in.
  </p>

  <p class="cta">
    <a href="/gallery#soft-life">Browse the Self Love wallpapers &rarr;</a>
  </p>
</ChromeLayout>

<style>
  h1 {
    font-size: var(--t-title1-size);
    font-weight: var(--t-title1-weight);
    letter-spacing: var(--t-title1-track);
    margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
  }
  .lead {
    font-size: var(--t-lead-size);
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
  }
  p {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .cta {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }
  .cta a {
    font-weight: 600;
  }
</style>
